meta {
  name: 07_PartyKinds
  seq: 7
}

docs {
  Scenario: The kinds of subject the endpoint resolves

    When a service owner looks up a self identified user
    Then only that user's own party is returned, typed as self identified
    When the subject is an ID-porten user registered by email
    Then the party carries the email identifier
    When the subject is a rightholder with access packages
    Then the firm is returned with the packages delegated to that person
    When the subject is a rightholder that has been given nothing
    Then the list is empty, since a rightholder relation on its own authorizes nothing
    When the subject is a system user
    Then the organisation the system user was created for is returned

  On this endpoint the kind is a property of the SUBJECT in the request body, not of the
  caller. The caller is always the same service owner.
}
